1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Ahhhhhhh!

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Nice observation skills.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
You really are quite the animal.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Regardless, it's already over now.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Over? What is?

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:09,000
You've fulfilled your purpose here.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Take your leave, Radies, before the other knights arrive.

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
It's little Oster, right?

12
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Don't worry, I promise to kill you soon enough!

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,000
And make a plaything of your corpse!

14
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Something we can both look forward to, you brat!

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Spatial magic is still magic!

16
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,000
And I've still got my sword!

17
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
I'm gonna hack that spell to pieces!

18
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,000
The hell?

19
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
That hurts!

20
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,000
You're gonna pay for that, you little wretch!

21
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Unfortunate.

22
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:54,000
You're whining about a little cut, after the pain you've caused!

23
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
You want pain?

24
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,000
I'll give you pain!

25
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
You tortured innocent people and laughed the whole time!

26
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,000
So what should I do?

27
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
I can't afford to lose Radies just yet.

28
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
How pitiful.

29
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
I come here after receiving word from the Master.

30
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Only to arrive and find you fighting this?

31
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Pitiful indeed.

32
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,000
So now there's five of them?

33
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
This curse I've got on me.

34
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
None of these scrapes and scratches will stop bleeding.

35
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Looks like the tables have finally turned!

36
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
I move.

37
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Ones in a long way.

38
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,000
This is the only one.

39
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,000
So few of our elders.

40
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:33,000
hello

41
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:56,500
Yeah, yeah!

42
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:57,060
Yeah, yeah!

43
00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:59,740
Honestly I apologize's saloon

44
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:08,460
Mm hmm, mm hmm

45
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:33,280
It's gotten a lot quieter out there.

46
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:34,900
Is the invasion over?

47
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:40,940
It's so good.

48
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:41,780
It's so good.

49
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:42,580
It's so good.

50
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,280
It's so good.

51
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:44,320
I can't move.

52
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:49,060
Oh, my beautiful savior of sustenance.

53
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:55,980
I wonder what happened to those knights who saved me.

54
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,420
I hope they're okay.

55
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:11,600
Hosta!

56
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:12,960
What was that?

57
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:14,580
Small surgery.

58
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:17,080
Now I'm ready to fight again.

59
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:19,100
Watch.

60
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:20,900
I'll prove it to you.

61
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:23,100
Seriously?

62
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:27,280
Did he just strike himself with his own blades to dispel the curse?

63
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:28,520
Unbelievable!

64
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:30,460
Who would do that?

65
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:33,080
This kid's funny.

66
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:35,080
Can I pretty please dissect him later?

67
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,540
Be quiet and focus.

68
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:39,320
Phooey, you're no fun.

69
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,040
Here's the thing.

70
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:47,700
I've been fighting an uphill battle since I was born.

71
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:50,460
No matter how many guys you've got,

72
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,900
and no matter what you do to me,

73
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:56,580
I'll cut right through every last one of you!

74
00:05:57,280 --> 00:05:58,640
You hear me?

75
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:01,800
Let's see what you've got!

76
00:06:02,420 --> 00:06:05,300
Has the threat of our superior numbers driven him mad?

77
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:06,900
What's it matter anyway?

78
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,480
I can still dissect a crazy person.

79
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:17,720
Such a pointless flailing about.

80
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:20,900
The brat doesn't know when to give up!

81
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:25,960
Oh, I know who you are.

82
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:29,100
This must be the anti-magic boy the Master mentioned.

83
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:38,480
Your brash fearlessness may well be the greatest weapon you have,

84
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:40,340
but you must learn to remain calm.

85
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:44,280
That is, if you truly do wish to be the Wizard King.

86
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:53,740
You got it, Captain.

87
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:55,260
I can do calm.

88
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:58,660
I'm gonna calmly tear you to pieces!

89
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,440
Not likely.

90
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:02,380
Flame magic!

91
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:04,560
Exploding flame!

92
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:11,340
You think I'm gonna let you get away with what you did to my brother?

93
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:14,560
One of us is going down today, and it's not gonna be me!

94
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,420
How you doing, Asta?

95
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:19,060
You got room for one more?

96
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:19,900
Sure thing!

97
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:22,260
Feel free to jump in whenever you want to!

98
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:34,400
They fight like wounded beasts,

99
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:36,600
cornered with nothing left to lose.

100
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,400
They're fearless!

101
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:42,300
What are you waiting for?

102
00:07:42,380 --> 00:07:43,920
Just get rid of these idiots already!

103
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,580
What do you think we're doing?

104
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
This wasn't our original objective.

105
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:53,140
But you've made yourselves targets!

106
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:57,540
Thanks, Noelle!

107
00:07:57,760 --> 00:08:00,760
If those fools thought I'd let them kill my friends that easily,

108
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:02,160
then they were sorely mistaken!

109
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:02,660
Hey!

110
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:09,820
That's some pretty spiffy defensive magic!

111
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:11,360
Interesting.

112
00:08:12,140 --> 00:08:14,500
This girl has the look of the Royal House Silver.

113
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:16,180
Well, in that case,

114
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:19,540
we should respond with something appropriate to her exalted station.

115
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,580
Tree creation magic!

116
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,640
Magic draining roots!

117
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:33,780
Master!

118
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:34,920
I got it!

119
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:36,880
What are you planning to do?

120
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:43,580
Oh, no!

121
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:45,860
His counterspell swallowed up the torrent!

122
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:54,720
Admirable battle instincts,

123
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:56,420
but it won't be enough!

124
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:58,080
Wind creation magic,

125
00:08:58,380 --> 00:08:59,820
death by tornado needles!

126
00:08:59,820 --> 00:09:08,880
He was too fast!

127
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:10,340
Are you okay?

128
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:11,540
Please say something!

129
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:13,920
Now,

130
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:15,840
to finish this for good.

131
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:19,480
I can't help.

132
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:22,480
Please, no!

133
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:28,260
Ooh, how fun!

134
00:09:28,340 --> 00:09:30,440
I've never since magic like this before!

135
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:40,500
What?

136
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,540
You're back!

137
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:43,240
The rest of the magic knights!

138
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:43,600
No!

139
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:48,380
Did you think a little distance would be enough to save you?

140
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:49,860
You're back.

141
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:52,400
How from so far?

142
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:54,920
We work together to effect our return.

143
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:58,500
The cooperation doesn't come naturally to us.

144
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:00,460
If I had to give this spell a name,

145
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:02,760
I'd call it Super Compound Magic.

146
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:07,260
Merging our talents rather than vying for dominance.

147
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,440
What a novel idea!

148
00:10:09,060 --> 00:10:11,480
Well, I guess we can't write off men entirely, huh?

149
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:12,200
Yes.

150
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:14,560
It appears they can be useful on occasion.

151
00:10:15,220 --> 00:10:18,360
This cooperation business leaves a bad taste in my mouth.

152
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:21,980
We Silver Eagles have never been known for playing well with others.

153
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:22,720
And yet,

154
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:26,500
it is the duty of all magic knights to protect the kingdom.

155
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:29,780
If we must work together to do that, then so be it.

156
00:10:30,560 --> 00:10:31,720
What happened here?

157
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:33,200
He's badly hurt.

158
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:34,440
Do you think you can help?

159
00:10:34,580 --> 00:10:35,280
How horrible!

160
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:38,440
Who could do this to a man as strong as Captain Fugolion?

161
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:38,620
Come on!

162
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:48,800
Somebody check the others!

163
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:49,940
Are they still breathing?

164
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:51,380
Come on, Asta!

165
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,260
Wake up for me!

166
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:54,320
Good!

167
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:55,000
He's alive!

168
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:58,140
To have brought down fighters as strong as these three,

169
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,680
how powerful are they?

170
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:06,160
Our losses will be too high if we continue this fight.

171
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:07,400
Retreat!

172
00:11:08,060 --> 00:11:09,660
What leaving so soon?

173
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:11,080
Mercury Magic!

174
00:11:11,620 --> 00:11:12,720
Reign of Silver!

175
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:15,240
Gel Magic!

176
00:11:15,820 --> 00:11:17,640
Go Sticky Salamander!

177
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:22,040
It will take a far more powerful spell than that to withstand my Silver Rain.

178
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:23,240
Think so?

179
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,520
Dark Magic Item!

180
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:28,020
Property Boost Absorb!

181
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:29,220
Woohoo!

182
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:31,520
That's impossible!

183
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:34,060
It's soaking up the Captain's magic like it's nothing!

184
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:35,320
But how?

185
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,800
What sort of magic item is that?

186
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:42,920
Asta!

187
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:44,940
And gotcha!

188
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:46,940
What do you plan to do with him?

189
00:11:47,260 --> 00:11:48,280
It's a secret!

190
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:52,320
We'll leave you for now.

191
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:55,140
But remember this day, Magic Knights.

192
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:58,580
We are the Eye of the Midnight Sun.

193
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:02,500
And we will bring the Clover Kingdom to its knees!

194
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:10,060
Asta!

195
00:12:18,060 --> 00:12:18,540
Gel Magic!

196
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:20,940
Go Sticky Salamander!

197
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:25,320
It will take a far more powerful spell than that to withstand my Silver Rain.

198
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:26,520
Think so?

199
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:28,820
Dark Magic Item!

200
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:31,240
Property Boost Absorb!

201
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:34,800
That's impossible!

202
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:37,380
It's soaking up the Captain's magic like it's nothing!

203
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:38,640
But how?

204
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:41,120
What sort of magic item is that?

205
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:46,200
Asta!

206
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:48,200
And gotcha!

207
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:50,160
What do you plan to do with him?

208
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:51,280
It's a secret!

209
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:55,580
We'll leave you for now.

210
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:58,440
But remember this day, Magic Knights.

211
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:01,880
We are the Eye of the Midnight Sun.

212
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:06,040
And we will bring the Clover Kingdom to its knees!

213
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:13,320
Asta!

214
00:13:13,320 --> 00:13:16,500
They took Asta!

215
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:17,880
But he...

216
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,560
Let's follow them!

217
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:20,060
Stop, Noel.

218
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,100
It won't work.

219
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:21,840
Why not?

220
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:26,060
We have no means of tracking them and no way to know what awaits us if they are found.

221
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:27,400
I don't care!

222
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:28,240
Let it go.

223
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:32,200
Our priority right now is strengthening the Royal Capital's defenses.

224
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:34,960
For all we know, there could be more enemies about.

225
00:13:35,740 --> 00:13:38,800
We have neither time nor magic to waste on somebody like him.

226
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:42,360
How is Fuegolion?

227
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:43,560
Will he survive?

228
00:13:43,860 --> 00:13:46,600
I've done all I can with my magic, but it won't be enough.

229
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:51,460
We need to get him to the medical ward for more advanced healing spells as soon as we can!

230
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:52,760
We don't have much time!

231
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:55,540
A one-armed squad, Captain.

232
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:57,640
Is there any sight more pitiful?

233
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:01,280
This is what House Fuegolion has become?

234
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:03,780
It almost makes me ashamed to be a royal.

235
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,180
How could you say that?

236
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:07,100
The Captain fought bravely.

237
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,840
Because we are magic knights.

238
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:11,680
If we do not win, we may as well not exist.

239
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,940
Trying counts for nothing?

240
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:15,360
Less than nothing.

241
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,340
The Crimson Lion Kings are ruined now.

242
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:18,020
Enough, Solid!

243
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:22,000
We weren't here to fight, and that makes us even less than him.

244
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:24,060
Now see to the town's defenses.

245
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:26,600
This is no time for your adolescent posturing.

246
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:27,920
Right.

247
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:31,780
There's some sort of spell blocking transmission magic.

248
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,900
The chain of command is in chaos.

249
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:38,000
That explains why outside reinforcements never arrived.

250
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:39,620
Everyone stay sharp!

251
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:41,900
We need to secure the perimeter.

252
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:43,080
Keep your eyes open.

253
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:45,020
You bet, Char!

254
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:46,180
Call me Captain, Sol.

255
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:48,540
Okay, securing the perimeter, Captain Char.

256
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:50,660
At the right things are going,

257
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:53,140
I don't know when I'm ever going to have time for that dessert.

258
00:14:53,900 --> 00:14:54,520
Quick, Klaus.

259
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:55,220
Go.

260
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:56,920
Return to HQ for backup.

261
00:14:57,380 --> 00:14:57,720
Right.

262
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:03,360
Hasta.

263
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:03,440
Hasta.

264
00:15:16,180 --> 00:15:21,940
Raides, you put your petty need for revenge ahead of the mission, and this is the result.

265
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:25,840
The Master may have taken a liking to you, but don't get cocky.

266
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:31,860
Mocking about with those creatures of yours, taking on the Captain by yourself, you're an arrogant fool.

267
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:33,280
Give it a rest already.

268
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:37,760
If you had stuck to the plan like you were supposed to, things would have been much less complicated.

269
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:42,900
I don't see what you have to complain about when it was my precious puppets that were the victims of all of this.

270
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:46,900
Let's not forget about Catherine. Things didn't turn out too well for her either.

271
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:50,860
As if I care about that old hag.

272
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,020
Quit squabbling.

273
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:55,280
I don't know why everyone's so upset you got what you wanted, right?

274
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,980
Oh, and Sally, one thing.

275
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:00,760
This little prize of yours can't come with us.

276
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:01,600
Kill him.

277
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:02,440
What?

278
00:16:02,660 --> 00:16:03,760
You've got to be kidding.

279
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:06,340
